1
00:00:07,720 --> 00:00:10,060
Battle for the Red Stone of Asia,

2
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:16,440
JoJo versus Wamuu in a
one-on-one chariot duel!

3
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:20,820
The time is upon us.

4
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:26,500
When the full moon once again emerges from
behind that cloud, the battle will begin!

5
00:00:33,020 --> 00:00:35,437
I wish they wouldn't make all that noise?

6
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:38,257
Why is it that the bad
guys get all the fans?

7
00:00:38,340 --> 00:00:40,537
One lap is 960 meters.

8
00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:45,097
It takes approximately one minute
for these beasts to complete a lap.

9
00:00:45,180 --> 00:00:46,997
Do you see that column over there?

10
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:50,897
On each lap a different weapon
will be hanging from it.

11
00:00:50,980 --> 00:00:52,277
Weapons.

12
00:00:52,360 --> 00:00:55,697
No one.

13
00:00:55,780 --> 00:00:56,956
Weapon at at a time.

14
00:00:57,280 --> 00:00:59,757
Whichever of us can capture
that column before the

15
00:00:59,840 --> 00:01:03,193
other will then have the
opportunity to wield the weapon.

16
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:05,400
Do you see the first one up there?

17
00:01:05,740 --> 00:01:07,380
It's a giant sledgehammer.

18
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:14,671
That thing could smash right
through a chariot in one blow.

19
00:01:14,820 --> 00:01:19,880
If wamuu was able to get his hands on it,
my situation isn't just going to be bad?

20
00:01:20,100 --> 00:01:21,520
it could be terminal.

21
00:01:23,260 --> 00:01:25,960
But if I can get to it first,

22
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:30,660
cover it with oil and fill it with
Hamon, then victory will be mine.

23
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:35,860
I am looking forward to an excellent,
fulfilling fight from you, Jojo. Get ready.

24
00:01:40,960 --> 00:01:43,660
The moon approaches the cloud's edge.

25
00:01:43,900 --> 00:01:46,800
When its light falls upon
us, the contest begins.

26
00:01:49,780 --> 00:01:51,604
Jojo, what are you doing there?

27
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:53,500
The race is about to start.

28
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:55,980
I'm well aware of that.

29
00:01:56,480 --> 00:02:00,217
The start will be the key, and I
sure don't want to mess that up.

30
00:02:00,300 --> 00:02:03,237
That's why I'm checking
the rubble under my wheels.

31
00:02:03,320 --> 00:02:04,620
Look at that, Wamuu.

32
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:07,157
You've got quite a big
pile under your buggy.

33
00:02:07,240 --> 00:02:09,181
Are you going to take care of it?

34
00:02:14,380 --> 00:02:15,340
Hurry!

35
00:02:15,740 --> 00:02:17,152
Come on, get's up there!

36
00:02:25,320 --> 00:02:26,280
Jojo!

37
00:02:30,960 --> 00:02:32,720
Begin now!

38
00:02:51,160 --> 00:02:53,960
Thank you.

39
00:03:17,640 --> 00:03:20,440
Thank you.

40
00:04:08,860 --> 00:04:09,690
Hi-yah!

41
00:04:12,960 --> 00:04:13,920
What's this now?

42
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:16,360
Lord Wabu is having trouble!

43
00:04:16,620 --> 00:04:18,679
His chariot is just standing there!

44
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:22,100
Look at that, his wheels are blocked.

45
00:04:23,380 --> 00:04:25,080
Jojo, he did this.

46
00:04:25,320 --> 00:04:26,780
The cheeky little devil.

47
00:04:27,020 --> 00:04:28,060
You bastard!

48
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:32,317
You piled them there while we turned
our attention to watching the moon.

49
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:34,380
You are nothing but a cheater!

50
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:36,180
A rotten human cheater!

51
00:04:36,600 --> 00:04:39,997
Show me in the handbook where it
says I can't do something like that.

52
00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:44,177
All you told me was to lose means to die,
and that was the only rule in this fight.

53
00:04:44,260 --> 00:04:47,580
When it comes to my survival,
I don't care who I offend.

54
00:04:48,220 --> 00:04:49,050
Beep, beep.

55
00:04:49,540 --> 00:04:50,370
Hiya!

56
00:04:52,300 --> 00:04:53,130
Yah!

57
00:05:00,080 --> 00:05:03,637
The human's getting close
to the column! Yah! Get him!

58
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:05,014
Don't let him get him!

59
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:08,212
JoJo will be the first one to the hammer.

60
00:05:09,960 --> 00:05:14,720
Yes yes yes yes I can't wait
to have you in my grasp.

61
00:05:16,520 --> 00:05:22,620
I've got you you're mine damn I'm going
a lot faster than I thought I was!

62
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:28,997
Now stay there Jojo it snagged
my ring couldn't have predicted

63
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:34,120
that great that was lucky now
the The fight is in the bag.

64
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:35,260
I've got this.

65
00:05:35,620 --> 00:05:37,040
You can have the hammer.

66
00:05:37,760 --> 00:05:40,172
That was my plan from the very beginning.

67
00:05:43,100 --> 00:05:45,600
I see Wamuu has a plan in mind.

68
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:47,940
Let me see it now.

69
00:05:48,180 --> 00:05:49,533
You're fighting genius.

70
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:53,220
A little oil up here, add some pommel.

71
00:05:54,320 --> 00:05:57,438
I've got a little medicine
for you right here, Wamuu.

72
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:04,485
Wamu's starting to lose speed.

73
00:06:04,940 --> 00:06:06,237
It's not a race.

74
00:06:06,320 --> 00:06:08,277
They are in a fight to the death.

75
00:06:08,360 --> 00:06:11,297
The keys to winning are
tactics and strategy.

76
00:06:11,380 --> 00:06:13,197
The right weaponry.

77
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:15,257
Control of the environment.

78
00:06:15,340 --> 00:06:16,877
All right then.

79
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:21,372
I'll just slow down and introduce him
to my little friend here, the hammer.

80
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:25,477
Jojo, listen, you mustn't
slow down anymore.

81
00:06:25,560 --> 00:06:29,501
Since you're the one with the
hammer, I'll just get something else.

82
00:06:33,600 --> 00:06:37,300
So, Wamu, are you ready to see
exactly what this thing can do?

83
00:06:37,560 --> 00:06:38,680
Then here we go!

84
00:06:43,760 --> 00:06:44,680
Look there!

85
00:06:45,020 --> 00:06:48,432
He was so happy with his hammer
at first, but not anymore!

86
00:06:48,620 --> 00:06:51,320
He sure plans ahead better than I do!

87
00:06:52,400 --> 00:06:53,230
Hurry up!

88
00:06:53,313 --> 00:06:55,535
Go faster and get away from him, Jojo!

89
00:06:56,280 --> 00:06:57,400
Too late!

90
00:07:02,940 --> 00:07:06,220
So now, you will no
longer have your chariot.

91
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:11,700
Down already?

92
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:14,039
Things seem to be over a bit early.

93
00:07:16,580 --> 00:07:19,000
He might want to rethink his plan.

94
00:07:22,160 --> 00:07:22,990
Jojo!

95
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:28,917
The probability of him being
trampled by my vampire horses is 90%.

96
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:32,837
The chance of him attempting
to break left is 5%,

97
00:07:32,920 --> 00:07:35,997
and breaking to the right is 5%.

98
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:40,400
So now then, what is our little
human warrior going to do?

99
00:07:42,620 --> 00:07:43,537
My hammer.

100
00:07:43,620 --> 00:07:44,980
Where is my hammer?

101
00:07:45,300 --> 00:07:46,520
He wants his hammer?

102
00:07:46,760 --> 00:07:48,417
Did he hit his head too hard?

103
00:07:48,500 --> 00:07:50,853
That hammer's not going to save you now!

104
00:07:51,860 --> 00:07:53,620
Jojo must not dodge.

105
00:07:53,920 --> 00:07:58,240
If he does, Wamuu will stop and
finish him with his divine sandstorm.

106
00:07:58,580 --> 00:08:03,860
But what Jojo did was grab the hammer
and head straight for Wamuu's chariot.

107
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:07,300
Well done, Jojo. Great thinking.

108
00:08:07,580 --> 00:08:08,940
That's exactly right.

109
00:08:12,780 --> 00:08:13,610
What?

110
00:08:13,693 --> 00:08:16,267
He struck the yoke midway
between the horses.

111
00:08:17,540 --> 00:08:23,100
As the horses ran on, Jojo used the hammer's
force to launch himself into the sky.

112
00:08:25,040 --> 00:08:26,880
That move was unbelievable.

113
00:08:27,340 --> 00:08:31,277
The hammer's life kept him from being
trampled under the hooves of the horses.

114
00:08:31,360 --> 00:08:32,540
How was that?

115
00:08:34,900 --> 00:08:39,020
And now for that big hammer
whack you worked so hard to earn.

116
00:08:40,620 --> 00:08:41,580
He's gone.

117
00:08:42,060 --> 00:08:43,060
Where'd he go?

118
00:08:44,300 --> 00:08:48,260
You can clearly see that Wamu
is a step ahead of his quarry.

119
00:08:52,040 --> 00:08:53,200
Wait, that's right!

120
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:56,734
These fellas can hide themselves
inside other creatures!

121
00:08:59,240 --> 00:09:00,070
Ha-ha!

122
00:09:00,300 --> 00:09:01,340
That was close!

123
00:09:02,320 --> 00:09:04,160
His boot came off his foot!

124
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:05,717
That boot saved him!

125
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:08,506
If he only had on some
other kind of footwear!

126
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:11,777
I've got luck on my side!

127
00:09:11,860 --> 00:09:15,777
For example, the way the handle of
that hammer got caught on my ring.

128
00:09:15,860 --> 00:09:17,625
Luck helps with effectiveness.

129
00:09:18,060 --> 00:09:20,413
Now let's take a look at your situation.

130
00:09:21,180 --> 00:09:24,577
Wamu, your own power has trapped
you inside of that horse.

131
00:09:24,660 --> 00:09:26,020
That's not very lucky.

132
00:09:28,860 --> 00:09:30,580
And here we go.

133
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:35,200
A little hum on for you and the
horse you rode in on. You fool.

134
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:36,793
You don't see the trap.

135
00:09:37,320 --> 00:09:38,300
Careful, Jojo.

136
00:09:38,560 --> 00:09:40,854
You need to keep an arm's leg from him.

137
00:09:44,840 --> 00:09:48,577
Now that Wamuu has merged with that
horse, he's free to use his hands!

138
00:09:48,660 --> 00:09:51,131
without worrying about vibration or speed.

139
00:09:51,520 --> 00:09:52,677
Which means, then...

140
00:09:52,760 --> 00:09:55,584
No one has survived a
direct hit by that attack.

141
00:09:55,860 --> 00:09:56,860
Caesar couldn't.

142
00:09:57,060 --> 00:10:00,500
And now you will taste Divine Sandstorm!

143
00:10:19,580 --> 00:10:22,457
Even if it lasted only the
distance of half a lap,

144
00:10:22,540 --> 00:10:25,720
it was a battle filled with
many twists and surprises.

145
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:30,457
But in the end, Wamu proved the
superiority of both his thinking?

146
00:10:30,540 --> 00:10:32,040
and his fighting prowess.

147
00:10:34,700 --> 00:10:38,229
I think the next battle is going
to be quite a test of will.

148
00:10:38,960 --> 00:10:41,784
Truly, it is not my
preference to fight a woman.

149
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:44,480
Wamu dislikes it even more.

150
00:10:45,820 --> 00:10:49,460
Notwithstanding, all users of
Hamon must be done away with.

151
00:10:51,860 --> 00:10:52,800
Drink that.

152
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:57,417
It will provide a painless death thanks

153
00:10:57,500 --> 00:11:00,017
that's quite considerate
of you but Jojo seems

154
00:11:00,100 --> 00:11:01,917
to be a little less dead than you thought

155
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:05,640
huh Lord course look
out there in the arena

156
00:11:08,940 --> 00:11:10,220
It can't be

157
00:11:10,900 --> 00:11:14,840
Lord Wamu's arms They look
like they're about to fall off

158
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:20,670
Madness

159
00:11:21,360 --> 00:11:24,240
How could this have
possibly happened to me?

160
00:11:25,560 --> 00:11:26,480
What's wrong?

161
00:11:26,740 --> 00:11:32,280
What is happening to Wamu out there?
Look! There! It's Jojo! He's alive!

162
00:11:32,560 --> 00:11:33,500
He's moving!

163
00:11:33,740 --> 00:11:35,200
He's not even hurt!

164
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:41,360
Well, I apparently managed
to survive once again.

165
00:11:41,780 --> 00:11:45,660
But Wamuu hit him directly with
his divine sandstorm attack.

166
00:11:46,100 --> 00:11:47,320
How could he?

167
00:11:47,980 --> 00:11:48,810
Directly?

168
00:11:49,840 --> 00:11:53,657
Jojo was cunning enough to make
it look like it was a direct hit.

169
00:11:53,740 --> 00:11:57,300
He is an absolute genius at
trickery and misdirection.

170
00:11:57,540 --> 00:12:00,834
But I'm not sure I should be
giving him praise for that.

171
00:12:01,920 --> 00:12:04,500
Take a close look at Wamuu's arms.

172
00:12:07,440 --> 00:12:09,440
Oh, wait, now I see.

173
00:12:12,800 --> 00:12:16,976
He wrapped the reins around Wamuu's
arms after filling them with Hamon.

174
00:12:18,020 --> 00:12:20,820
Wamuu's divine sandstorm
was short-circuited.

175
00:12:21,620 --> 00:12:24,497
Wamuu was already sticking
one hand out of the horse.

176
00:12:24,580 --> 00:12:27,237
He was going to try to
use his divine sandstorm.

177
00:12:27,320 --> 00:12:31,277
However, in order to do so, I knew he'd
have to stick his other hand out too.

178
00:12:31,360 --> 00:12:34,000
And I had the perfect
counter for that move.

179
00:12:34,620 --> 00:12:36,680
Lord Wamu's face! Look at him!

180
00:12:36,860 --> 00:12:38,720
He's in agony! See that?

181
00:12:38,940 --> 00:12:41,037
He doesn't seem to know where he's going!

182
00:12:41,120 --> 00:12:42,296
His eyes are vacant!

183
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:43,520
What should we do?

184
00:12:43,960 --> 00:12:45,500
It's the second lap!

185
00:12:45,820 --> 00:12:47,408
But what's going to happen?

186
00:12:47,660 --> 00:12:50,140
Lord Wamu can't hold a weapon like that!

187
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:52,780
Is it even possible for him to fight?

188
00:12:53,080 --> 00:12:54,560
It's not a surprise.

189
00:12:55,360 --> 00:12:59,817
Right in mid-attack, Wamu was
struck with a lethal dose of Homo.

190
00:12:59,900 --> 00:13:04,360
The confidence built up over
millennia of triumph has crumbled.

191
00:13:05,520 --> 00:13:09,920
The quiet, calm intensity his
victories gave him has vanished.

192
00:13:11,020 --> 00:13:13,380
A tragic shock for him.

193
00:13:13,920 --> 00:13:15,940
But it matters not at all.

194
00:13:16,160 --> 00:13:18,920
Put out the next set of
weapons and do it now!

195
00:13:22,820 --> 00:13:24,680
Lord Kars has given the order.

196
00:13:24,980 --> 00:13:26,980
When he speaks, we must obey!

197
00:13:31,220 --> 00:13:34,640
For the second lap, both
warriors will receive crossbows.

198
00:13:35,360 --> 00:13:37,880
Each comes with ammunition for two shots.

199
00:13:38,340 --> 00:13:42,164
The first warrior there has the
choice of the small or large bow.

200
00:13:54,160 --> 00:13:55,240
What's this now?

201
00:13:55,420 --> 00:13:56,457
There's two weapons.

202
00:13:56,540 --> 00:13:59,305
There's a large one and
another that's smaller.

203
00:14:00,420 --> 00:14:03,837
Lisa, Lisa, this is what's
going through your thoughts now.

204
00:14:03,920 --> 00:14:07,038
Wamuu's mind is in no
condition to entertain a fight.

205
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:11,077
So why then would Kars be
deploying these new weapons,

206
00:14:11,160 --> 00:14:13,160
and with such apparent confidence?

207
00:14:13,620 --> 00:14:15,960
It's very unsettling, is it not?

208
00:14:16,300 --> 00:14:21,660
Well, the reason is that at his core, Wamuu
is a warrior of legendary mental power.

209
00:14:22,260 --> 00:14:26,966
The very best athletes use a psychological
technique called the Switch Comeback.

210
00:14:27,680 --> 00:14:31,917
When these champions are brought low by
the pressure of shock, failure, or fear,

211
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,597
they can flip a mental
switch and bring out their

212
00:14:34,680 --> 00:14:37,386
fighting spirit for one
last Herculean effort.

213
00:14:37,720 --> 00:14:43,180
Desperate times call for desperate
measures, and Wamuu will win at any cost!

214
00:14:45,280 --> 00:14:46,920
No, I don't believe it!

215
00:14:47,120 --> 00:14:49,100
Did he really just do that? What?

216
00:14:49,280 --> 00:14:50,400
No, Lord Wamuu!

217
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:52,120
Look, his eyes are gone!

218
00:14:52,420 --> 00:14:54,460
He poked out his eyes!

219
00:14:56,760 --> 00:15:00,320
I foolishly relied on my eyes
because I was able to see,

220
00:15:00,520 --> 00:15:02,700
and Jojo exploited my weakness.

221
00:15:05,780 --> 00:15:10,200
Now I will use this horn to see things
outlined in wind instead of light.

222
00:15:14,140 --> 00:15:17,760
He flipped the switch by removing
his eyes from the equation.

223
00:15:18,040 --> 00:15:20,864
Now he is once again
psychologically invincible.

224
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:24,780
He senses the wind with
that horn on his forehead.

225
00:15:25,700 --> 00:15:29,140
He sees air better than he did light. Huh?

226
00:15:29,320 --> 00:15:30,967
What is that supposed to be?

227
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:33,711
That's not going to have any effect on me.

228
00:15:35,260 --> 00:15:37,613
Because of you, I lost my friend Caesar.

229
00:15:37,860 --> 00:15:39,213
Try any trick you want.

230
00:15:39,300 --> 00:15:42,006
I'll do whatever it takes
to finish the fight.

231
00:15:42,840 --> 00:15:45,040
Jojo, which crossbow will you take?

232
00:15:45,140 --> 00:15:46,081
Yeah, which one?

233
00:15:46,220 --> 00:15:47,220
You need to ask.

234
00:15:47,400 --> 00:15:49,047
You know the answer to that.

235
00:15:49,700 --> 00:15:52,160
The large one, you stupid morons.

236
00:15:52,460 --> 00:15:53,820
Power is what I want.

237
00:15:55,520 --> 00:15:58,040
You gotta admit that one does have power.

238
00:15:58,280 --> 00:16:00,020
Yeah, lots of power.

239
00:16:02,040 --> 00:16:03,240
Oh, come on!

240
00:16:03,480 --> 00:16:05,320
I can't even draw this thing.

241
00:16:05,860 --> 00:16:09,560
It's so tight, I can't get the
string to go anywhere at all.

242
00:16:11,080 --> 00:16:11,910
You like it?

243
00:16:11,993 --> 00:16:13,357
You got greedy, didn't you?

244
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:17,440
Even a normal crossbow takes a huge
amount of strength to draw back.

245
00:16:17,680 --> 00:16:19,621
You had to have the big one, huh?

246
00:16:19,900 --> 00:16:21,540
That's what greed gets you.

247
00:16:27,940 --> 00:16:31,293
I will use the first ball to
paint a picture of the wind.

248
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:43,320
Now that I know what the range
is, the next shot will not miss.

249
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:47,277
How am I supposed to defend myself
if I can't shoot this thing?

250
00:16:47,360 --> 00:16:48,980
Lord Wobble, shoot him!

251
00:16:49,180 --> 00:16:50,620
